function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    print("<div class=\"doc-detail-layout\"><main class=\"content doc-page doc-detail\"><h2>component_exists</h2><div class=\"doc-section signatures\"><h3>Capy</h3><pre>function component_exists(name : string) bool</pre></div><div class=\"doc-section content\"><h3>Description</h3><p><code>component_exists()</code> runs the same name resolution that <code>component()</code> and <code>component_render()</code> use, and reports whether it found a file. It renders nothing and runs no handler.</p><p>Use it to make a component optional. Without the guard, a missing component sets the response status to <code>500</code> and writes a banner element into your page; with it, you choose the fallback.</p><h2>What the check does and does not cover</h2><p>It resolves the <strong>file</strong>. A <code>:HANDLER</code> suffix is ignored for the purpose of this check, so <code>component_exists(&quot;widgets.capy:CARD&quot;)</code> answers &quot;does <code>widgets.capy</code> exist&quot;, not &quot;does it define <code>COMPONENT:CARD</code>&quot;. A name whose file exists but whose named handler does not will pass this check and then fail at render time.</p><p>It also does not compile the component. A file that exists but does not compile returns <code>true</code> here and reports its compile error when it is rendered.</p><p>Resolution is unchanged from <code>component()</code>: <code>.capy</code> is appended when absent, a leading <code>/</code> is tried as a real path and then as a site-root path, and a relative name is tried against the entry unit&#39;s directory, the calling unit&#39;s directory, and the site root, in that order.</p></div><div class=\"doc-section params\"><h3>Parameters</h3><div><p>name : a component path, optionally followed by <code>:HANDLER</code></p></div><div></div></div><div class=")
    print("\"doc-section\"><h3>Return Values</h3><p><code>true</code> when Bearer resolves the name to a component source file, otherwise <code>false</code>.</p></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">if component_exists(&quot;/doc/examples/card.capy&quot;) { print(&quot;exists\\n&quot;) } else { print(&quot;missing\\n&quot;) }\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">if component_exists(&quot;/doc/examples/card.capy&quot;) {\n    component_render(&quot;/doc/examples/card.capy:CARD&quot;, {title: &quot;Themed&quot;})\n} else {\n    print(&quot;&lt;p&gt;Default header&lt;/p&gt;&quot;)\n}\nprint(&quot;\\n&quot;)\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">var candidates := [&quot;/doc/examples/missing.capy&quot;, &quot;/doc/examples/card.capy&quot;]\nfor candidate := candidates {\n    if component_exists(candidate) {\n        print(candidate, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n    }\n}\n</pre></div></div></main><aside class=\"doc-section see-also\"><h3>See also</h3><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/component/\">component</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/component-render/\">component_render</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/component-resolve/\">component_resolve</a></aside></div>")
}
